1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:04,510
(Sheldon:)Good evening.

2
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:07,540
(Sheldon:)I'm your guest lecturer,
Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

3
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:16,500
(Sheldon:)I was expecting applause,

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,290
(Sheldon:)but I suppose stunned silence
is equally appropriate.

5
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,950
(Sheldon:)I agreed to speak
to you this evening,

6
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:26,120
(Sheldon:)because I was told that you're
the best and the brightest

7
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:28,360
(Sheldon:)of this university's
doctoral candidates.

8
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:30,340
(Sheldon:)Hmm. Of course,
that's like saying

9
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:33,650
(Sheldon:)you are the most important
electron in a hydrogen atom.

10
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,070
'Cause, you see,

11
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:43,440
(Sheldon:)there's only one electron
in a hydrogen atom.

12
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:47,750
(Sheldon:)Best and brightest,
my sweet patootie.

13
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:49,410
(Sheldon:)All right, let's begin.

14
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:51,830
(Sheldon:)Show of hands,
who here is familiar

15
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:54,490
(Sheldon:)with the concept
of topological insulators?

16
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:56,990
(Sheldon:)Don't kid yourselves.

17
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:01,960
(Leonard:)I found another tweet from a
student at Sheldon's lecture.

